## 8. Memory envelope and responsiveness (3 GB target)

**[Inference, bounded by W2-exec and S7]** Reading strategy: never decode the whole file; serve the viewport from C2's tile cache (default cap 1 GiB) reading only touched tiles via tifffile's tile/zarr access [S7]. The 3 GB case (60000×25000 uint16) is 1475 tiles of 2 MiB; a full second in-RAM copy would be 3.00 GB — so the design budget is one tile cache, no full-image buffers, masks composited per-viewport. **W2-exec (executed micro-check)**: under a seeded pan-with-5%-jump trace, LRU hit rates were 14.6 % (64 MiB), 19.8 % (256 MiB), 43.0 % (1 GiB). Interpretation: bounded memory is easy, *smoothness is not free* — hence pyramid-level selection (serve zoomed-out views from downsampled levels, generating them as a recorded resample operation) and prefetch are minimum-adjacent requirements, not polish [L4]. Cancellation: cooperative tokens checked per tile/chunk; progress = tiles done / estimated. Annotation updates touch only the in-memory geometry + segment append, so they stay interactive independent of image size.

**Limits:** W2 is a synthetic trace in a sandbox — it demonstrates the memory arithmetic and the cache-size sensitivity, not measured fps on real hardware [scope limits in witnesses.json].

