## 9. UX obligations (minimum)

- **Keyboard operability**: all tools reachable and usable from the keyboard (pan/arrows, zoom/±, slice/time PgUp/PgDn, tool hotkeys, Enter/Esc for polygon commit/cancel); no mouse-only action. [Choice; accessibility requirement from brief.]
- **Legible metadata/error feedback**: a log panel (not toast-only) rendering import warnings, unresolved sources, and export manifests in plain text; high-contrast theme; error text states *what* failed, *which file*, and *what to do*. [Choice.]
- **Styles**: named annotation styles reusable across sessions (§4.3). **Undo/redo**: command-pattern, per-entry, deep history within session; journal records nothing user-visible loss on undo (undo is view-level history, journal is committed provenance).
- **Original vs derived**: layer tree marks entries `source`/`derived`; derived entries list their operation chain on hover/status bar.
- **Export honesty**: every export carries a sidecar manifest (space, units, origin, source sha256, operation chain, lossy mappings applied) — directly modeled on QuPath's documented "units and origin" contract and its named lossy mappings (ellipses→polygons; overlap order) [S6].

