## 11. Validation summary

Executed by candidate (isolated component checks only): **W1c** transform-convention arithmetic (passed; superseded failed attempts W1a/W1b disclosed), **W2** cache-budget simulation (passed; informative). Proposed/UNEXECUTED: W3 tifffile axis/calibration readback; W4 kill-9 recovery; W5 float32 drift; W6 NGFF clause verification; W7 GeoJSON RFC conformance; W8 cross-machine reopen; W9 napari release-tag confirmation. No executed check establishes full-application behavior.

## 12. Critical assumptions and unsupported cases

Assumes: TIFF-family dominance in the group's corpus (validates against a real file census early — [W3]); POSIX rename atomicity on the shared storage (verify on the actual NAS — some SMB/NFS setups disable it; fallback: manifest swap with backup file, [W4-extension]); single-writer-per-project (bundle exchange, not live co-editing, per brief). Unsupported in v1: non-TIFF/PNG proprietary formats, live acquisition streams, >RAM annotation masks, orientation matrices (retained verbatim, not applied), DICOM, cloud/storage services, automatic segmentation, registration. Where evidence remained uncertain — NGFF clause text [W6], first shipping release of the napari fix [W9], shared-drive rename semantics — the plan names the bounded fallback instead of assuming success.
